affection.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:06.459
'Trump didn't seem to realize
Pompeo hadn't actually seen

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:07.760
Kim Jong-un during the trip,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.396
asking if Pompeo had handed
the CD, wrote Bolton.

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:11.496
'Pompeo had not.

00:07:11.496 --> 00:07:12.765
Getting this CD to Kim

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.133
remained a high priority
for several months.'"

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:17.870
Okay. First of all, I love that
it was a CD in the year 2018.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.706
Knowing Trump, his plan was to
get Kim Jong-un to pay a penny

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.209
for that and 11 other CDs
and then have him on the hook

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.378
for the rest of his life.
"Classic, Columbia House."

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:29.147
Second, it's so weird to give
someone an autographed copy

00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:30.849
of a CD that isn't yours.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:33.351
For Christmas one year
I gave my mom "Wolf Hall"

00:07:33.351 --> 00:07:35.187
but I didn't sign it.

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:38.457
So a con artist warmonger is
cashing in by detailing horrific

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.492
abuses of power by a con
artist president

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:41.861
subverting our democracy,

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:44.263
and all the while the Republican
Party is just standing by,

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:45.331
letting it happen.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.699
We're all watching right now

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:49.602
as our institutions fail us
in a time of acute crisis.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:51.737
Police are beating protesters
with impunity,

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.773
a deadly pandemic
is ravaging the nation,

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:56.275
and unemployment is higher
than it's been in a century.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:58.277
And many people who
thought the government

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.580
would be there to protect them
are learning that it's not.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.916
It's like being on an airplane
and assuming the oxygen mask

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.152
will be there in an emergency,
and then you hit some turbulence

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:08.454
and the only thing that comes
down is a voucher that says,

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:10.322
"We know you have many
choices when you fly.

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:12.991
Thank you for choosing us,
and please, rest in peace."

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:15.427
And in many ways, the various
crises we're experiencing

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:17.629
right now are connected
in at least one sense.

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:20.900
The structural inequality and
the institutional failures

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.236
laid bare by the coronavirus
pandemic helped set the stage,

00:08:24.236 --> 00:08:27.773
in part, for the unprecedented
mass demonstrations

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.409
against systemic racism
and police brutality.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:34.079
-I think we were primed for
this moment by the coronavirus.

00:08:34.079 --> 00:08:38.150
By a lot of the American
mythology being laid bare.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:41.988
One, the idea we can be
relentlessly upwardly mobile

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:44.956
and that white folks have
sort of their grasp

00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:46.191
on the American dream.

00:08:46.191 --> 00:08:47.660
When the economy shut down

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.060
and people realized they were

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:51.664
two paychecks away
from destitution

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.599
and the government may
not be there for them,

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.501
there was a sense of
vulnerability

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.303
and a physical vulnerability.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:09:00.806
And then as we saw, the
coronavirus made people

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.274
lean into their neighbors.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:05.944
Once you tap into that source of
vulnerability, interdependence,

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:08.614
humanity and and awareness
of inequality

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:11.417
that the coronavirus
has exposed,

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.753
you're primed for
something big.

00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:15.420
-She's right.
The pandemic made the

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.222
failures of our institutions
very real

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:18.691
for tens of millions of people.

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:21.894
And in turn, it led to a deep
sense of community solidarity.

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:23.329
People had to look out
for each other

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:25.030
because they realized the
government wouldn't,

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.733
by checking on neighbors,
supporting local businesses,

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.702
and liking your friends'
Instagram pics

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:31.003
of their janky banana bread,

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:32.804
even though they have already
posted half a dozen

00:09:32.804 --> 00:09:35.107
banana bread pics, and they are
not getting any better.

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:37.410
You're over-mixing
the batter, Steven.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.477
[ Sighs ]

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:39.711
Your bananas aren't
ripe enough.

00:09:39.711 --> 00:09:42.548
It [bleep] breaks my heart
to tell you that, Steve.

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:45.183
Your bananas aren't
ripe enough, bro,

00:09:45.183 --> 00:09:47.152
and you're embarrassing
yourself on social media.

00:09:47.152 --> 00:09:49.421
People are discovering that
their government just isn't

00:09:49.421 --> 00:09:52.591
there for them, thanks in part
to years of concerted efforts

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:53.692
by the moneyed class

00:09:53.692 --> 00:09:55.293
and the corporate elite
to hollow it out.

00:09:55.293 --> 00:09:58.097
If every year you pump trillions
into corporate tax cuts

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.431
and the military and cut
everything else,

00:09:59.431 --> 00:10:01.000
you're gonna end up with a
country where millions of

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.668
people don't have jobs
or healthcare,

00:10:02.668 --> 00:10:04.236
billionaires are doing great,
and everyone else

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:06.605
is met with tear gas
and riot gear.

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:08.940
I mean, think of what else we
could be spending money on

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:11.209
right now instead of tanks for
local police departments.

00:10:11.209 --> 00:10:13.479
And even if you really want to
spend the money on tanks,

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:15.047
the least you could do
is give them to nurses

00:10:15.047 --> 00:10:17.049
and postal workers
instead of the police.

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:19.685
If instead of a tiny little
mail car, every postal worker

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:21.854
had a tank,
they would make damn sure

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:23.956
you got that Pottery Barn
catalog.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:26.157
In fact, one small thing we
could keep spending money on

00:10:26.157 --> 00:10:28.460
are the additional unemployment
benefits provided by

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.328
the coronavirus
stimulus package.

00:10:30.328 --> 00:10:32.531
As you might recall,
the bill added $600

00:10:32.531 --> 00:10:34.800
to unemployment benefits,
which Republicans

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.535
tried to get rid of at the time,

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:39.104
a move that enraged
Bernie Sanders.

00:10:39.104 --> 00:10:42.874
-And now I find that some of
my Republican colleagues

00:10:42.874 --> 00:10:45.511
are very distressed.
They are very upset

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:48.514
that somebody who is making
10, 12 bucks an hour

00:10:48.514 --> 00:10:53.151
might end up with a paycheck
for four months

00:10:53.151 --> 00:10:55.787
more than they received
last week.

00:10:55.787 --> 00:10:59.925
Oh, my God, the universe
is collapsing.

00:10:59.925 --> 00:11:01.794
Imagine that.

00:11:01.794 --> 00:11:04.663
Somebody who's making
12 bucks an hour,

00:11:04.663 --> 00:11:09.769
now like the rest of us, faces
an unprecedented economic crisis

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:13.639
with the 600 bucks on
top of their normal,

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:15.674
their regular unemployment check

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:20.179
might be making a few bucks
more for four months.

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:22.047
Oh, my word.

00:11:22.047 --> 00:11:24.282
Will the universe survive?

00:11:24.282 --> 00:11:25.851
-Say you what you will about
Bernie, but we really missed

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:28.220
An opportunity for some
grade A old man sarcasm

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.488
in the debates with trump.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:30.923
Oh, the media is mean to you?

00:11:30.923 --> 00:11:32.358
How will the universe survive?

00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:33.592
You know what we used to do

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:35.094
when someone was mean
to us back in my day?

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:36.428
We didn't tweet.
We rode our bikes

00:11:36.428 --> 00:11:37.962
down to the sandlot
and challenged them

00:11:37.962 --> 00:11:38.997
to a game of baseball.

00:11:38.997 --> 00:11:41.199
On Sunday, Trump
economic adviser

00:11:41.199 --> 00:11:44.136
Larry Kudlow said the Trump
administration would cut off

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:47.739
the additional $600 because
it somehow disincentivizes

00:11:47.739 --> 00:11:49.641
people from going back to work.

00:11:49.641 --> 00:11:53.979
-The federal government
program for unemployed Americans

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:57.482
gives them an extra $600
a week in benefits.

00:11:57.482 --> 00:12:00.185
But it's slated to
run out in six weeks.

00:12:00.185 --> 00:12:02.287
Now, obviously the health
effects and economic effects

00:12:02.287 --> 00:12:03.955
are going to last
longer than that.

00:12:03.955 --> 00:12:07.226
Should American families that
are receiving these extra

00:12:07.226 --> 00:12:13.165
$600 checks right now expect
that money to stop in August?

00:12:13.165 --> 00:12:16.268
-Well, unemployment benefits
will not stop in August.

00:12:16.268 --> 00:12:22.274
What may well stop -- and this
reform is necessary -- almost

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:25.410
all businesses, frankly,
on both sides of the aisle,

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.079
or mostly both sides
of the aisle,

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:31.216
understand that the $600
plus up, that's above

00:12:31.216 --> 00:12:33.986
the state unemployment benefits
that they will continue

00:12:33.986 --> 00:12:37.222
to receive is, in effect,
a disincentive.

00:12:37.222 --> 00:12:39.425
I mean, we're paying
people not to work.

00:12:39.425 --> 00:12:41.726
It's better than their
salaries would get.

00:12:41.726 --> 00:12:44.830
-I don't know. I think that says
less about unemployment benefits

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.498
and more about how
little we pay workers,

00:12:46.498 --> 00:12:48.667
you senile business egg.

00:12:48.667 --> 00:12:51.369
Also, I love that he thinks all
these people are on a salary.

00:12:51.369 --> 00:12:53.172
Oh, so you're a driver
for Papa John's?

00:12:53.172 --> 00:12:55.407
What is that, 100k a
year in stock options?

00:12:55.407 --> 00:12:57.409
I bet you get stock options,
I presume.

00:12:57.409 --> 00:13:00.412
So you think we're paying
people not to go to work?

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:03.115
We're paying them because our
sociopathic government failed

00:13:03.115 --> 00:13:04.583
to protect them from
a deadly disease,

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.384
and our barbaric capitalist
system

00:13:06.384 --> 00:13:07.553
has rendered
them expendable.

00:13:07.553 --> 00:13:09.755
Not everyone can spend
their day golfing

00:13:09.755 --> 00:13:11.590
and watching TV like
the guy you work for.

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:14.159
if we're paying anyone
not to work, it's him.

00:13:14.159 --> 00:13:17.262
The only way Trump could watch
more TV is if golf courses

00:13:17.262 --> 00:13:20.165
started putting tiny screens
in the bottom of the cup.

00:13:20.165 --> 00:13:21.866
The people at the top are
stuffing their hands

00:13:21.866 --> 00:13:24.203
in the till, trying to cash out
before everything burns down.

00:13:24.203 --> 00:13:27.505
And meanwhile, they won't even
let you keep an extra $600 bucks

00:13:27.505 --> 00:13:29.608
a week during a pandemic
they failed to stop.

00:13:29.608 --> 00:13:32.211
I've got to be honest, sometimes
it really does feel like --

00:13:32.211 --> 00:13:34.746
-The universe is collapsing.

00:13:34.746 --> 00:13:36.515
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:39.985
♪♪

00:13:39.985 --> 00:13:41.420 line:0%
As New York struggles
to re-open,

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.288 line:0%
remember that we're
still a city in crisis,

00:13:43.288 --> 00:13:44.489 line:0%
and City Harvest has been

00:13:44.489 --> 00:13:45.991 line:0%
stepping up to meet
the increased need.

00:13:45.991 --> 00:13:48.894 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:13:48.894 --> 00:13:51.597 line:0%
Stay safe, wash your hands,
we love you.

